kosha copper

  -- Cu. proton-29. period 4, transition metal. valence: 1 or 2.
  -- excellent electrical and thermal conductor — used in wiring, heat exchangers.
  -- antimicrobial: bacteria cannot survive on copper surfaces (oligodynamic effect).
  -- Cu²⁺ in enzymes: cytochrome c oxidase (respiration), tyrosinase (melanin).
  -- alloys: brass (Cu+Zn), bronze (Cu+Sn) — the Bronze Age material.
  -- blue-green patina: Cu + O2 + CO2 + H2O → Cu2(OH)2CO3 (malachite).
  -- second only to gold in electrical conductivity among common metals.

